runtime-cube-armv7.tar.gz

What it is: the unmodified Android Widevine L3 libraries of an Amazon Fire TV
Cube (2nd generation, Android 9, 32-bit ARM): vendor/lib/libwvhidl.so, the
Android system libraries it needs, and the Android linker. 21 files, listed with
their sizes and SHA-256 sums in runtime-manifest.json inside the archive.

Who made it: Google (Widevine) and Amazon. These files are not covered by
CoreTube's BSD-3-Clause license. They are shipped as the official libraries for
this purpose, as confirmed by the developer.

What it does not contain: no provisioned profile, device certificate, license or
key. Each box asks Google's provisioning server for its own fresh L3 certificate
the first time it plays protected video, and keeps it only on that box
(Kodi add-on data: browser.tizentube/android-drm). Never add that folder, or any
file from it, to this repository or to an add-on zip.

How it was made: drm/tools/copy_runtime.py, which mounts the Cube's Android
partitions read-only and copies the files unchanged. Check it with:

  python3 drm/tools/runtime_bundle.py check drm/runtime/runtime-cube-armv7.tar.gz
